<title>UK: UK c/a deficit seen at 4.25 bln stg in 97-Treasury.</title>
<headline>UK c/a deficit seen at 4.25 bln stg in 97-Treasury.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The UK Treasury said in its &quot;Red Book&quot; financial statement and budget report that the current account deficit was expected to be 2.25 billion stg in 1996, rising to 4.25 billion stg in 1997.</p>
<p>Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke had previously forecast a 3.5 billion stg deficit for the current year in his summer forecasts released in July.</p>
<p>(See separate summary of key economic forecasts, which will be issued shortly)</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
